A||||8||theogre||Site additions
Z||000000||theogre||05-15-99||06:33 PM||||Cliff and I have been talking about some of the future of the site, Some one once mentioned a picture area.<p>A couple of the things Cliff and I talked about were a FAQ, and a tips area. I've already written a few pages for cliff to post as soon as he gets time. Once they are up, any one else who wants to write something should feel free to do so. (I say once they are up because I'd hate to see someone put allot of time into something that's already covered.)<p>I'd like to know what things people think should go into a FAQ. For starters, I'd like to make it more useful, I.E. better written than the "Online Service Guide" that has moved all over the web. I'd also like to see sections writen by some of the forums regulars. We've got a growing number of people here that actually know something, unlike most of the other forums that can't even find some decent software to run the forum. <p>Ideally I'd like to see a page for each question and it's answer. Especially since the really usefull answers to many questions can be fairly long. (As we've seen in the forum) I would like most, if not all answers, to be a colaberative effort. We have people who know how to do things, but writing about how to do things is a whole diferant ball of wax.<p>An example question might be:<p>What is the "tach filter?" Where is it and why is it the first thing you should check if you are having ignition problems?<p>As most of you know,,, that one item could fill a book with the things it can do to drive you nutty.
Z||000001||theogre||05-17-99||07:14 AM||||No one else has any comment or ideas? 
Z||000002||LEE498||05-17-99||11:34 AM||||Yes yes, you guys got a good thing going here ,It's actually better than you might think.This is the great 'fiero forum' and it's becoming more popular by the day.There's more technical info given out here more than anywhere i know of. You guy's have done a great thing ,and pictures will make it better. What ever you guy's decide to do i'm for it.   
Z||000003||LEE498||05-17-99||11:38 AM||||Yes yes, you guys got a good thing going here ,It's actually better than you might think.This is the great 'fiero forum' and it's becoming more popular by the day.There's more technical info given out here more than anywhere i know of. You guy's have done a great thing ,and pictures will make it better. What ever you guy's decide to do i'm for it.   Being able to post a ? and have 5-10 people try and help you is really something else man!! That's where it's at!!!
Z||000004||Patrick||05-17-99||03:13 PM||||<br>Sorry Ogre, we're not ignoring you.<p>Regarding pictures at this site, I believe the reason we <b>haven't</b> seen many pictures posted so far is because most of us DON'T have our own web page to link to when we want to share our images with others. For any kind of a "picture area" to take off, maybe there needs to be some easy to follow instructions regarding acquiring one's own web page. There are "free" web pages available (<b>Geocities</b> comes to mind), so it would be great if someone in the know could inform us on how to follow through with this.<p>Your suggestion of having a page dedicated to each question is fine, except of course, for the problem of having to find someone to do all the writing. Yes, if everyone handled one question it would be wonderful, but would that be the case? <p>I have to admit that part of the appeal of a forum such as this for me is the way that the questions are posted and answered. In each thread we hear from up to a dozen people. Each person has their own solution and their own writing style. It's fascinating to watch a long thread "evolve". I enjoy seeing how the threads go off in different directions. The frustrating part is finding something when you know that it's been mentioned before. If I may be as bold as to cut and paste something from an earlier post of mine, here's a suggestion:<p>"The "commercial" version (of Ultimate Bulletin Board) also has a <b>Search</b> function which comes in real handy when trying to find something which has already been discussed in an earlier thread. I appreciate the fact that this "freeware" version (used here) probably doesn't support that feature, but it's something to keep in mind when there are hundreds and hundreds of posts to wade through at this forum in the future."<p>I'm noticing more and more now that "newbies" at this site are asking about topics that have already been covered. It eventually gets tiring to have to dredge up the same answers over and over again. I'm sure you especially know what I'm talking about. It might not only be easier to have a <b>Search</b> function instead of a rewritten, dedicated, question and answer page, but it might also be less "dry". If we could have both, well, that would be even better.<p>The other thing that I've mentioned before, is that I'd like to be able to go back and correct my posts after I've submitted them. Again, the "commercial" version of <b>Ultimate</b> supports this, I don't know about the "freeware" version. I know I probably take these things much too seriously, but am I the only one here who has a hemorrhage when they screw up their post? <IMG SRC="http://forums.gagames.com/forums/biggrin.gif"> <p>Whatever you and Cliff decide to do is fine by me. You've both done a fine job up till now.<p> 
Z||000005||theogre||05-17-99||03:48 PM||||for the record.... the site is entirly Cliff's. I'm mostly looking for input on things to write about. For the articles I write in their entirty, I keep the copy rights. For articles I'm going to do for the FAQ area, I'm going to put them into public domain.<p>I don't expect allot of people to write. I thought a perminant area for some items might be good.<p>I'm not sure what all Cliff has on the server. There may be a way to make a CGI form that would allow the creation of a user profile with pictures outside ultimate. I know you can do a guest book type of thing, but I'm not sure how you could add pictures to one.<p>Yes, The comercial version of ultimate does a bunch of stuff this version doesn't do. That version also cost a fair amount of change. Cliff is already putting out a signifigant amount of cash every month for this site. I don't know what's the budget like, but expect it's pretty tight.
Z||000006||RFMike||05-17-99||05:44 PM||||I am a new participant in the Forum, but I have read all the available posts.  It appears there are a lot of threads regarding bushings and suspension improvements, engine swaps, and ignition problems.  I know that each of these subjects can and do take books to cover, but some general info for each would be a good starting point for someone who has just arrived.<br>I am also in favor of search capabilities.  I don't know the software costs, but I would be willing to contribute.  You've already saved me money.  The most important and most expensive part of a mechanic's fee is diagnosis.  Even a hack like me can swap parts.  I know a lot of you are accomplished diagnosticians.  I'm not, and I appreciate the help, in any form it comes in.
Z||000007||RFMike||05-17-99||05:56 PM||||Oh, yeah, it would be nice for a newby to be able to download all the posts, and read offline, rather than flipping back and forth from topic to topic.  On the other hand, maybe everyone isn't as fanatical as myself. Ah, I bet they are.
Z||000008||theogre||05-17-99||08:24 PM||||well.......... time allowing, I usually check things here a few times a day. (BTW I live in the U.S. Cliff and the site are in Holland.)<p>Part of the huge growth in readership here is a direct result of using ultimate for the system. the rest is people willing to write answers in a usable form. There is no other forum that is close to this usefull. The major reason is bad software that drives off users. places who use "guest book" CGI's just can't compare. The only other site that is even remotely usefull, and ogre supported, is Pontiac Fiero Knowledge Base.<p>I'll help to manage/edit a FAQ but I don't want to write every thing in it. I think you all will like most of what I've written so far, as soon as cliff gets to post it, but there's only so much time available to me. I just don't have time to write books. I don't even have time to add a section to the Ogre Cave for Fiero right now.  <A HREF="http://home.sprynet.com/sprynet/theogre" TARGET=_blank>home.sprynet.com/sprynet/theogre</A> <p>Part of the reason I want to write a diferant page for each FAQ item is to make it downloadable, and as time allows, to make it searchable by adding a CGI to the server. Having the FAQ as an area outside the ultimate system makes this fairly simple.<p>In order for this to work, I will need all you to help. I know allot of stuff. I don't know everything. I also tend to write on a more technical level than many people are comfortable with.<p>As soon as I get a chance, I'll post all the generic text of the stuff i've written to the ogre cave as a new section. That way the "regulars" can review the text even before Cliff gets time to post it. This way I can get your feed back and save Cliff some time with repeated updates.
